WEBVTT

00:00:00.714 --> 00:00:02.664
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you go out on Friday night?

00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:09.450
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> Yes, my husband Eddie and I always go out for a drink or for dinner.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.626
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where do you go?

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:17.285
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> We usually go to our local pub, because they have good food there.

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:20.445
We sometimes meet friends there, too.

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:23.834
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What time do you get up on Saturday and Sunday?

00:00:24.438 --> 00:00:31.987
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> On Saturday at seven thirty. On Sunday it depends. At about nine?

00:00:32.266 --> 00:00:34.768
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you usually do on a Saturday?

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:41.769
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> I work from nine to four. I’m a hairdresser and we’re open on Saturdays.

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:48.438
Then after work I go to the supermarket and buy food for the week.

00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:53.417
In the evening, we usually stay at home and watch TV.

00:00:54.461 --> 00:00:59.848
My husband’s a big football fan and he always watches Match of the Day.

00:01:00.807 --> 00:01:02.878
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where do you usually have lunch on Sunday?

00:01:03.255 --> 00:01:06.986
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> With my parents, or sometimes Eddie’s parents.

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:12.207
My dad makes a very good Sunday lunch – he’s the cook in the family.

00:01:12.323 --> 00:01:14.401
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Are you tired on Sunday evening?

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:23.642
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> Yes, because in the afternoon we need to do housework. Cleaning, washing, things like that.

00:01:24.036 --> 00:01:27.011
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you do the same thing every weekend?

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.469
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> Yeah – more or less. Except when we’re on holiday.

00:01:32.943 --> 00:01:35.032
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What’s your favourite part of the weekend?

00:01:35.912 --> 00:01:37.872
<v><b>Kat:</b></v> Friday night, definitely!